  "plain": "In 1967 a man named Thomas Baron, hired by NASA, the US space agency, to judge how likely its programme was to succeed, was killed by a train, and his 500-page report then vanished. That is how Joe Rogan, a guest on the show, tells it, passing on Baron's story as he heard it. Rogan tells it to suggest that someone who had written a damning report was silenced and the report buried."
